  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Emergency Response to conflict-affected populations in Northern Mozambique</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">For over four years, the province of Cabo Delgado in Mozambique has experienced brutal attacks by armed groups, while neighbouring provinces of Nampula, Niassa, Zambezia, and Sofala are seeing a spill over of displacement. The humanitarian situation continues to deteriorate in both hosting and displaced communities, and for those left behind. In this project, IOM is supporting conflict-affected populations in Northern Mozambique through Water Sanitation and Hygiene (WASH) assistance.</narrative>
  </description>
